Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 10:29:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 14/23] Metal: floor-anchored kernel window (ducc0's placement)

A support-s kernel covers distances (-s/2, s/2], so the footprint must be
anchored on floor(u): cells floor(u)-s/2+1 .. floor(u)+s/2. Rounding to the
nearest cell instead dropped the cell at distance ~s/2 for half the
visibilities - up to 2.6% of the weight at support 6 - which is a systematic
~1% amplitude deficit. Fixed in all four polynomial kernels, the degridding
kernel, and the host-side tile bucketing (a visibility must be listed in every
tile its window touches).

The probe's float64 twin shared the flaw, so only the image-level harness could
see it.

